# Learning in the &quot;Neural&quot; Organisation.

**Authors:** Hutchin, Ted

## Abstract
Argues that methods of organizational communication and learning resemble neural networks and that developing teaching methods to reflect this understanding should be crucial. Provides an overview of neural organization, the application of neural networks to organizational structure, and education and training within organizations. Concludes that organizational learning should be learner centered. (PEN)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ536081

